{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790564613836,"sessionID":"ses_f1a087aeaffe6drfnH5MZxc2OA","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_UxHdqNy3WLR4qUoMuJO4U0qP","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/community_workshop_replan/01_planning_rules.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/community_workshop_replan/01_planning_rules.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Planning Rules\n2: \n3: Effective date: 2026-06-03\n4: \n5: ## Source Reliability\n6: \n7: - Use the newest dated facility source for room availability when facility notes conflict.\n8: - Session requirements in `02_sessions.csv` control capacity, time block, equipment, and room-trait needs.\n9: - Room traits and base costs come from `03_room_options.csv` unless a newer facility update changes room availability.\n10: \n11: ## Hard Requirements\n12: \n13: - Assign every session to exactly one room.\n14: - Use rooms that are available for the session time block.\n15: - Room capacity must be at least the session attendee count.\n16: - If a session needs a projector, demo table, quiet room, or loading access, the assigned room must provide it.\n17: - Total room cost must be at or below `$800`.\n18: - Prefer the lowest-cost valid room for each session unless preserving a correct existing assignment after an update is more important.\n19: \n20: ## Replanning Rule\n21: \n22: If a coordinator update makes part of the initial plan invalid, repair only the affected part when possible. Preserve correct assignments that still satisfy all requirements.\n\n(End of file - total 22 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Planning Rules\n\nEffective date: 2026-06-03\n\n## Source Reliability\n\n- Use the newest dated facility source for room availability when facility notes conflict.\n- Session requirements in `02_sessions.csv` control capacity, time block, equipment, and room-trait needs.\n- Room traits and base costs come from `03_room_options.csv` unless a newer facility update changes room availability.\n\n## Hard Requirements\n\n- Assign every session to exactly one room.\n- Use rooms that are available for the session time block.\n- Room capacity must be at least the session attendee count.\n- If a session needs a projector, demo table, quiet room, or loading access, the assigned room must provide it.\n- Total room cost must be at or below `$800`.\n- Prefer the lowest-cost valid room for each session unless preserving a correct existing assignment after an update is more important.\n\n## Replanning Rule","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/community_workshop_replan/01_planning_rules.md","text":"# Planning Rules\n\nEffective date: 2026-06-03\n\n## Source Reliability\n\n- Use the newest dated facility source for room availability when facility notes conflict.\n- Session requirements in `02_sessions.csv` control capacity, time block, equipment, and room-trait needs.\n- Room traits and base costs come from `03_room_options.csv` unless a newer facility update changes room availability.\n\n## Hard Requirements\n\n- Assign every session to exactly one room.\n- Use rooms that are available for the session time block.\n- Room capacity must be at least the session attendee count.\n- If a session needs a projector, demo table, quiet room, or loading access, the assigned room must provide it.\n- Total room cost must be at or below `$800`.\n- Prefer the lowest-cost valid room for each session unless preserving a correct existing assignment after an update is more important.\n\n## Replanning Rule\n\nIf a coordinator update makes part of the initial plan invalid, repair only the affected part when possible. Preserve correct assignments that still satisfy all requirements.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":22,"totalLines":22,"truncated":false}},"title":"tasks/community_workshop_replan/01_planning_rules.md","time":{"start":1790564613812,"end":179