{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790564613845,"sessionID":"ses_f1a087aeaffe6drfnH5MZxc2OA","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_i5zPYzOsjbfuaauQoFI4q8M1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/community_workshop_replan/output_contract.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/community_workshop_replan/output_contract.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Deliverable Contract\n2: \n3: Create an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. Markdown tables or concise labeled sections are fine, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n4: \n5: ## `answer/initial_room_plan.md`\n6: \n7: Record the room assignment plan before any coordinator update is introduced.\n8: \n9: Required facts:\n10: \n11: - One row or entry for every session in `02_sessions.csv`.\n12: - The selected room for each session.\n13: - The room evidence that supports each assignment: capacity, time block, required equipment or room trait, and cost.\n14: - The initial total room cost and budget status against the `$800` ceiling.\n15: - Any backup room considered for a fragile assignment.\n16: \n17: ## `answer/update_response.md`\n18: \n19: After the coordinator update is introduced, explain what changed and how the plan should be repaired.\n20: \n21: Required facts:\n22: \n23: - The update source and date.\n24: - The specific room assignment affected by the update.\n25: - Which original assignments remain valid and should be preserved.\n26: - The replacement assignment and why it satisfies the same session requirements.\n27: - The revised cost effect.\n28: \n29: ## `answer/final_room_plan.md`\n30: \n31: Write the final room assignment package after applying the update.\n32: \n33: Required facts:\n34: \n35: - One final room assignment for every session.\n36: - The final total room cost and remaining budget.\n37: - A short note confirming the same workshop objective is still covered.\n38: - A short note naming preserved work from the initial plan.\n39: \n40: Rules:\n41: \n42: - Use local files only.\n43: - Do not put the required deliverables in the task root; put them under `answer/`.\n44: - Do not relax hard room requirements unless a local file explicitly says to.\n45: - Extra scratch files are allowed, but the three named deliverables under `answer/` are the review packet.\n\n(End of file - total 45 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Deliverable Contract\n\nCreate an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. Markdown tables or concise labeled sections are fine, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n\n## `answer/initial_room_plan.md`\n\nRecord the room assignment plan before any coordinator update is introduced.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One row or entry for every session in `02_sessions.csv`.\n- The selected room for each session.\n- The room evidence that supports each assignment: capacity, time block, required equipment or room trait, and cost.\n- The initial total room cost and budget status against the `$800` ceiling.\n- Any backup room considered for a fragile assignment.\n\n## `answer/update_response.md`\n\nAfter the coordinator update is introduced, explain what changed and how the plan should be repaired.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/community_workshop_replan/output_contract.md","text":"# Deliverable Contract\n\nCreate an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. Markdown tables or concise labeled sections are fine, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n\n## `answer/initial_room_plan.md`\n\nRecord the room assignment plan before any coordinator update is introduced.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One row or entry for every session in `02_sessions.csv`.\n- The selected room for each session.\n- The room evidence that supports each assignment: capacity, time block, required equipment or room trait, and cost.\n- The initial total room cost and budget status against the `$800` ceiling.\n- Any backup room considered for a fragile assignment.\n\n## `answer/update_response.md`\n\nAfter the coordinator update is introduced, explain what changed and how the plan should be repaired.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- The update source and date.\n- The specific room assignment affected by the update.\n- Which original assignments remain valid and should be preserved.\n- The replacement assignment and why it satisfies the same session requirements.\n- The revised cost effect.\n\n## `answer/final_room_plan.md`\n\nWrite the final room assignment package after applying the update.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One final room assignment for every session.\n- The final total room cost and remaining budget.\n- A short note confirming the same workshop objective is still covered.\n- A short note naming preserved work from the initial plan.\n\nRules:\n\n- Use local files only.\n- Do not put the required deliverables in the task root; put them under `answer/`.\n- Do not relax hard room requirements unless a local file explicitly says to.\n- Extra scratch files are allowed, but the three named deliverables under `answer/` are the review packet.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":45,"totalLines":45,"truncated":false}},"title":"tasks/community_workshop_replan/output_contract.md","time":{"start":1790564613828,"end":1790564613845}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_00a054a675dfd5ba016ab9d905b72c87d2aea6671f4c4cd178"}},"id":"prt_0e5f7bec3001rP0YS71I7BtvwP","sessionID":"ses_f1a087aeaffe6drfnH5MZxc2OA","messageID":"msg_0e5f7a50b001ssc4WsCOdj1VPr"}}
